       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than double the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. A 3,000 mg single dose is also three times the usual 1,000 mg maximum. That much acetaminophen risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total). This may be what you meant if \"3000\" was the daily total.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum). Many clinicians use a lower ceiling of 3,000 mg/day for long-term use or when there are hepatic risk factors.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 3000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
